<title>INDIA: India's EID Parry 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India's EID Parry 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     300.8   v   267.2</p>
<p>    Sales		  7,610.3  v  7,148.1</p>
<p>    Final div (rupees	2.5  v	2.1</p>
<p>    Interim div  (rupees)  1.5  v	1.5</p>
<p>    Other income	   203.5  v    200.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  7,047.5  v   6,846.0</p>
<p>    Interest		 227.4  v     105.5</p>
<p>    Gross profit	   538.9  v     396.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   193.1  v     129.4</p>
<p>    Tax			 45.0  v	--</p>
<p>Note:- EID Parry India Ltd is a leading manufacturer of fertilisers, sanitary ware and confectionary products. It said in a statement that production was affected due to a labour strike for a period of 34 days in its sugar factory and a lock-out for 77 days at its sanitary ware plant during the year.</p>
<p>EID Parry made a $40 million issue of global depositary receipts (GDRs) in July, 1994.</p>
</text>
